  "content": {
    "id": "p7-q7-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "7",
    "prompt": "Prove that\n$$\\begin{aligned}&(a-b)(a+b)+(b-c)(b+c)+(c-d)(d+c)\\\\&\\qquad=(a-d)(a+d).\\end{aligned}$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "The left-hand side simplifies to $a^2-d^2=(a-d)(a+d)$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}(a-b)(a+b)+(b-c)(b+c)+(c-d)(d+c)&=a^2-b^2+b^2-c^2+c^2-d^2\\\\(a-b)(a+b)+(b-c)(b+c)+(c-d)(d+c)&=a^2-d^2\\\\(a-b)(a+b)+(b-c)(b+c)+(c-d)(d+c)&=(a-d)(a+d).\\end{align*}$$\nThis is the right-hand side, so the identity is proved.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 40
  },
